--=-g/eTA7nuL7jP4EsHUdcZ
Content-Type: text/plain; charset="UTF-8"
Content-Transfer-Encoding: quoted-printable

I *frequently* waste a bunch of time when I take a 32-bit .config from a
test machine and try to build it on a faster 64-bit system, and its
existing setting of CONFIG_64BIT=3Dn gets *changed* to match the build host=
.

This is because the default setting for $ARCH when discovered from
'uname' is one of the legacy pre-x86-merge values (i386 or x86_64),
which effectively force the setting of CONFIG_64BIT to match. We should
default to ARCH=3Dx86 instead, finally completing the merge that we
started so long ago.

This patch preserves the behaviour of the legacy ARCH settings for commands
such as:

   make ARCH=3Dx86_64 randconfig
   make ARCH=3Di386 randconfig

... since making the value of CONFIG_64BIT actually random in that situatio=
n
is not desirable.

In time, perhaps we can retire this legacy use of the old ARCH=3D values.
We already have a way to override values for *any* config option, using
$KCONFIG_ALLCONFIG, so it could be argued that we don't necessarily need
to keep ARCH=3D{i386,x86_64} around as a special case just for overriding
CONFIG_64BIT.

We'd probably at least want to add a way to override config options from
the command line ('make CONFIG_FOO=3Dy oldconfig') before we talk about doi=
ng
that though.

Signed-off-by: David Woodhouse <David.Woodhouse@intel.com>
---
 Makefile                        | 3 ++-
 arch/x86/Kconfig                | 2 +-
 arch/x86/Makefile               | 4 ++++
 arch/x86/configs/i386_defconfig | 1 +
 4 files changed, 8 insertions(+), 2 deletions(-)

diff --git a/Makefile b/Makefile
index 6f07f4a..19ee030 100644
--- a/Makefile
+++ b/Makefile
@@ -165,7 +165,8 @@ export srctree objtree VPATH
 # then ARCH is assigned, getting whatever value it gets normally, and=20
 # SUBARCH is subsequently ignored.
=20
-SUBARCH :=3D $(shell uname -m | sed -e s/i.86/i386/ -e s/sun4u/sparc64/ \
+SUBARCH :=3D $(shell uname -m | sed -e s/i.86/x86/ -e s/x86_64/x86/ \
+				  -e s/sun4u/sparc64/ \
 				  -e s/arm.*/arm/ -e s/sa110/arm/ \
 				  -e s/s390x/s390/ -e s/parisc64/parisc/ \
 				  -e s/ppc.*/powerpc/ -e s/mips.*/mips/ \
diff --git a/arch/x86/Kconfig b/arch/x86/Kconfig
index 97f8c5a..54a2f69 100644
--- a/arch/x86/Kconfig
+++ b/arch/x86/Kconfig
@@ -1,7 +1,7 @@
 # Select 32 or 64 bit
 config 64BIT
 	bool "64-bit kernel" if ARCH =3D "x86"
-	default ARCH =3D "x86_64"
+	default ARCH !=3D "i386"
 	---help---
 	  Say yes to build a 64-bit kernel - formerly known as x86_64
 	  Say no to build a 32-bit kernel - formerly known as i386
diff --git a/arch/x86/Makefile b/arch/x86/Makefile
index e71fc42..5c47726 100644
--- a/arch/x86/Makefile
+++ b/arch/x86/Makefile
@@ -2,7 +2,11 @@
=20
 # select defconfig based on actual architecture
 ifeq ($(ARCH),x86)
+  ifeq ($(shell uname -m),x86_64)
+        KBUILD_DEFCONFIG :=3D x86_64_defconfig
+  else
         KBUILD_DEFCONFIG :=3D i386_defconfig
+  endif
 else
         KBUILD_DEFCONFIG :=3D $(ARCH)_defconfig
 endif
diff --git a/arch/x86/configs/i386_defconfig b/arch/x86/configs/i386_defcon=
fig
index 5598547..9444708 100644
--- a/arch/x86/configs/i386_defconfig
+++ b/arch/x86/configs/i386_defconfig
@@ -1,3 +1,4 @@
+# CONFIG_64BIT is not set
 CONFIG_EXPERIMENTAL=3Dy
 # CONFIG_LOCALVERSION_AUTO is not set
 CONFIG_SYSVIPC=3Dy
--=20
1.8.0.1


--=20
